# Feature branches from fresh main

Every new task must start from up-to-date `origin/main` on a dedicated git branch. Do **not** implement, commit, or push task work directly on `main`. Do **not** continue an old feature branch unless the user says this task belongs on that branch.

## Start of a task

1. Fetch: `git fetch origin`.
2. Update local `main`: `git checkout main` && `git merge --ff-only origin/main` (or `git pull --ff-only origin main`).
3. Create and switch to a new branch from that `main`, e.g. `git checkout -b short-topic-name`.
4. Use a short descriptive name (`fix-trip-upload`, `add-map-nav`, …).

Starting from stale `main` causes merge conflicts with work already merged (PRs, other chats). Always refresh first, even if you already have a local `main`.

## During the task

- Keep all commits on that branch.
- Do not merge to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Push the feature branch when the user asks to push (not `main` unless they say so).

## Exceptions

Only work on `main` if the user explicitly says to use `main` for that task.
